.TH AVR\-ORG\-INSTALL\-RUNNER\-SET 1 "" "avr 0.5.0" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-org-install-runner-set \- Verify and configure MACHINE_TYPE, replacing its previous runner if present.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr org install runner set
[OPTIONS] MACHINE_TYPE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verify and configure MACHINE_TYPE, replacing its previous runner if present.
.PP
Read the token from a hidden prompt or --runner-token-stdin.
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
JSON FIELDS
    architecture, configured, cpu_count, description, disk_gb,
    invalid_at, machine_type, memory_mb, paused, run_untagged,
    runner_id, status, tag, token_expires_at, verified_at
.fi
.RE
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIMACHINE_TYPE\fR
\&
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-org\fR \fITEXT\fR
Organization ID or slug. Uses default org if not specified (see: avr config set org).
.TP
\fB\-\-installation\-id\fR \fITEXT\fR
GitLab installation ID (ins-xxx format). (required)
.TP
\fB\-\-runner\-token\-stdin\fR
Read the runner authentication token from standard input.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-org-install-runner (1),
.BR avr-org-install-runner-create (1),
.BR avr-org-install-runner-delete (1),
.BR avr-org-install-runner-list (1)
